    <bpmn:process id="W_W5502" name="W5502. Employee Financial Wellness Program — Literacy Education, Salary-Linked Lender Governance &amp; Debt-Stress Support" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: (a) Program design/review cycle; (b) salary-linked lender onboarding or deduction-authorization request; (c) debt-distress indicators (EAP case mix, deduction-load spikes, post-calamity advance surges)
Frequency: Education campaigns quarterly; lender-governance review annual; counseling continuous via EAP; deduction operations continuous
Volume: 6,911 employees; Philippine salary-linked lending context (registered lending companies, digital salary-deduction apps, informal &#x27;5-6&#x27; exposure) makes deduction-load a chain-wide indicator — anonymized payroll data shows the concurrent-deduction distribution across ~200 stores/4 DCs/HQ; EAP financial-stress cases route from W2865
Owner: EAP Manager
Participants: HR Manager, Benefits (VS-102), Payroll (VS-19.2), Legal, IT/LMS (VS-19.4 training delivery), external financial-education provider, accredited credit counselors, LP/VS-125 (aggregate risk-indicator interface only)
Source: workflow W5502 — Employee Financial Wellness Program — Literacy Education, Salary-Linked Lender Governance &amp; Debt-Stress Support</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5502_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5502_Lane1" name="EAP Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5502_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5502_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5502_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5502_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5502_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5502_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5502_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5502_Lane2" name="Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5502_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5502_Lane3" name="Payroll">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5502_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5502_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5502_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5502_Start5" name="(a) Program design/review cycle; (b) salary-linked lender onboarding or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5502_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5502_Task6" name="Program design &amp; needs assessment: financial-wellness policy, segment needs…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Program design &amp; needs assessment: financial-wellness policy, segment needs (frontline store/DC, corporate, new hires, near-retirement) from anonymized EAP case mix, deduction-load distribution, and engagement survey items; annual plan and budget
Responsible (R): EAP Manager / HR
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 5–8 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5502_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5502_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5502_Task7" name="Financial literacy education: quarterly modules — budgeting, debt management…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Financial literacy education: quarterly modules — budgeting, debt management, saving, SSS/Pag-IBIG/PhilHealth benefits literacy, scam and predatory-lending-app awareness — via LMS with completion records (W51 pattern) plus store huddle kits for frontline reach (VS-63 delivery); BSP-aligned consumer-protection content standards
Responsible (R): EAP Manager / L&amp;D / External Provider
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 8–10 days/quarter (team effort)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5502_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5502_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5502_Task8" name="Salary-linked lender governance: maintain the accredited-lender list; require…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Salary-linked lender governance: maintain the accredited-lender list; require SEC registration/lending-company compliance (RA 9474), Truth-in-Lending disclosures (RA 3765), fair-collection attestations, and RA 10173 data-privacy terms (VS-91); annual re-vetting; delisting process for abusive collection practices
Responsible (R): Legal / EAP Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 5–8 days/year + per lender</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5502_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5502_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5502_Task9" name="Deduction operations interface: payroll executes salary-deduction instructions…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Deduction operations interface: payroll executes salary-deduction instructions only against a valid employee authorization on file with the accredited lender; process new/modified/revoked instructions with audit trail; remit collections to lenders with reconciliation; separation-time coordination with final pay (W43 pattern) so deductions stop cleanly
Responsible (R): Payroll / HR
Accountable (A): Payroll Manager
Duration: 30–60 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5502_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5502_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5502_Task10" name="Take-home-pay guardrail: monitor aggregate deduction load per employee; flag…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Take-home-pay guardrail: monitor aggregate deduction load per employee; flag cases exceeding the policy guardrail (multiple concurrent lender deductions eroding net pay) for confidential outreach through EAP — never through line management; monitor formal garnishments separately per VS-19.2 statutory process
Responsible (R): Payroll / EAP Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 0.5 day/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5502_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5502_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5502_Task11" name="Debt-distress identification &amp; support: referral pathways (self, manager, EAP…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Debt-distress identification &amp; support: referral pathways (self, manager, EAP counselor) into confidential financial-coaching sessions; navigation to W76 company loan/calamity-loan options where appropriate; referral to accredited credit counselors for debt restructuring; substance-abuse and mental-health interlocks where debt stress co-occurs (W2865/W2868/VS-150)
Responsible (R): EAP Manager / Counselors
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: Continuous; ~2–4 hrs/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5502_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5502_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5502_Task12" name="Crisis overlays: post-typhoon financial-first-aid sessions and calamity-loan…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Crisis overlays: post-typhoon financial-first-aid sessions and calamity-loan awareness in affected regions (VS-69.3); special modules when economic shocks (fuel/food inflation) spike deduction-load indicators
Responsible (R): EAP Manager / HR
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 2–3 days per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5502_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5502_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5502_Task13" name="Privacy &amp; safeguard interlocks: wellness data confidential and never used in…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Privacy &amp; safeguard interlocks: wellness data confidential and never used in performance or staffing decisions; only anonymized aggregate indicators shared (e.g., with LP under VS-125/VS-23 governance) and only at group level; DPIA maintained for program data (VS-91)
Responsible (R): EAP Manager / DPO-function / Legal
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 2–3 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5502_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5502_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5502_Task14" name="Measurement &amp; reporting: participation, EAP financial-case mix, deduction-load…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Measurement &amp; reporting: participation, EAP financial-case mix, deduction-load trends, W76 utilization, attrition correlation; annual ROI report feeding the wellness analytics cycle (W2872)
Responsible (R): EAP Manager / People Analytics
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 3–4 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5502_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5502_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5502_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5502_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5502_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-480 (ensure controlled execution — Mental Health, Wellness &amp; Employee Assistance Program (PA-83.3).)
Owner: EAP Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5502_Assoc17" sourceRef="W5502_Annotation16" targetRef="W5502_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
